  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.ctx.wire-test/many-red-tests-draw-a-summary-with-what-reads-the-rest}}
 {:seon.task/name "teaching-is-data"
  :seon.task/plan "The owner, 2026-11-05: the agent's entity \"teaches them about the system, it explain what task they are working on, how messaging works when they get a message, evertyhing. It's all data driven\"; \"NO SPECIAL CASE FOR CITING\"; \"NO OTHER MECHANISMS\".

What exists outside data: the system message is docs/prompt.md's text (seon.ctx.wire/system-text; on stage 2b's branch, sections named by :seon.agent/system); seon.model/eval-tool's descriptions teach how to evaluate; seon.ctx.session's session-open and the example session tags frame a session in fixed words; citing has writers of its own (seon.render.ui/page-cites, seon.task/agent-cites-tx, :seon.config.agent/cites, my.agent/cite! and uncite!); seon.ctx.wire/help-text and seon.learn are text beside the entity.

The change: what an agent reads is data on its entity, or on entities it refs, rendered by their schemas' renders: the prompt's sections by ref, how messaging works by the message's render, how a task is worked by the task's. eval-tool's descriptions say only the tool's shape. Citing is ordinary data and swap!. What an agent adds of its own is a key and a render (docs/ctx.md#adding-a-datum-and-its-render).

Deletes: session-open and the example tags' fixed words where a render can say them; page-cites, agent-cites-tx, :seon.config.agent/cites, my.agent/cite! and uncite!; help-text's copy of what the wiki holds.

Proofs: two agents with different data read different context with no code changed; the system message's words come from the entity's refs. Judged by real agents' turns to green (seon.ctx/context-makes-agents-better)."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{}}
 {:seon.task/name "context-makes-agents-better"
