 {:seon.task/name "the-models-readers-follow-the-re-models"
  :seon.task/plan "Context's readers that move when Optimization's re-models land (docs/users.md#the-stages-agreed-2026-11-09), each in the same branch as its schema change or right after it:
1. A run's measures are entities of their own, a ref to what they measured, summed when read (re-model 1, Optimization, on jolt/sync): seon.ctx.status's readers of :seon.test/ticks, :seon.test/bytes and :seon.fn/stats (status, task-of's :proved, the var pattern's :seon.test/* attributes) read the measures by their ref.
2. A cite's target is a ref to an entity that exists (Optimization, jolt/cite-ref in the erase window): the joins by value in the cite and task patterns (:proved, :section, :var, :callers, a cite's :task, :schema, :ns) become ref joins keyed by their attribute, and their readers in seon.ctx.status, seon.ctx.search, seon.render.ui's cite renders and my.agent/cites move; seon.ctx-test/a-pattern-joins-refs-by-their-attribute then holds no :by join.
3. seon.ctx's write! refuses an edit of a var through swap! by checking :var/name in code; instead a property on the var's and form's entity schemas says the entity is changed by its definition, and the edit walk reads it."
